From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:58:16 +0100
Subject: clk: send POST_RATE_CHANGE whenever PRE_RATE_CHANGE was sent

clk_propagate_rate_change() sends PRE_RATE_CHANGE when the predicted
new_rate differs from the current rate, but clk_change_rate() only
sends POST_RATE_CHANGE when the rate read back after the change
differs from the old one. When a clock can't produce the requested
rate exactly and ends up where it was, notifiers get PRE_RATE_CHANGE
without a matching POST_RATE_CHANGE.

This breaks notifiers that change hardware state on PRE_RATE_CHANGE
and restore it on POST_RATE_CHANGE, like the Rockchip fractional
divider notifier, which moves the frac mux to the fractional divider
for the duration of the change. On RK3588 the CRU node assigns
786432000 Hz to AUPLL, which already runs at 786431991 Hz, the closest
rate it can generate. The S/PDIF fractional dividers below it get
PRE_RATE_CHANGE (14945847 -> 14945848 Hz), their muxes are switched to
the fractional divider, and are never switched back. The clock
framework still believes the muxes select the integer divider, so the
S/PDIF controllers feeding DisplayPort audio run from a gated clock and
never request DMA.

Send POST_RATE_CHANGE whenever PRE_RATE_CHANGE was sent.
---
 drivers/clk/clk.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/clk.c b/drivers/clk/clk.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/clk.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk.c
@@ -2519,7 +2519,14 @@ static void clk_change_rate(struct clk_core *core)
 	if (core->flags & CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE)
 		clk_core_disable_unprepare(parent);
 
-	if (core->notifier_count && old_rate != core->rate)
+	/*
+	 * PRE_RATE_CHANGE was sent if the predicted new_rate differed from the
+	 * old rate. Send POST_RATE_CHANGE in that case too, even if the rate
+	 * the hardware ended up at is the old one, so that notifiers can undo
+	 * what they did on PRE_RATE_CHANGE.
+	 */
+	if (core->notifier_count &&
+	    (old_rate != core->rate || old_rate != core->new_rate))
 		__clk_notify(core, POST_RATE_CHANGE, old_rate, core->rate);
 
 	if (core->flags & CLK_RECALC_NEW_RATES)
-- 
